FUTURE - categories for CHOICE / MULTI_CHOICE lists (not scheduled -
needed once plugin preset browsers are built)
================================================================================
No new DataListId/DataArgKind/DataActionType needed - still a flat,
idx-enumerable list_at. TODO when built:
- DataChoice gains DATA_CHOICE_CATEGORY (1u << 1), alongside the existing
  DATA_CHOICE_LINKED (1u << 0) - a row with this bit set is a node to
  descend into, not a pickable leaf.
- DataActionReq gains a top-level field, sibling to `type`, OUTSIDE the
  per-action union: `uint64_t category_scope;` (0 = list root). Set by
  the UI while drilling; ignored by list_at for non-categorised lists.
  Must be a dedicated top-level field, not a reused union field (e.g. NOT
  add_choice.choice_value - collides with CONNECT's own union usage).
- CLI-side drilling: one more branch in the existing "on SELECTED"
  handling already used by helper_choice_list_step's callers - category
  row updates category_scope/resets cursor and re-browses; leaf row
  behaves exactly as today. Backing out (h/ESC) needs a small caller-
  owned breadcrumb stack (scope, cursor) per level, capped like ACTION_
  ARG_COUNT elsewhere in this CLI - no heap.
- A category node's DataChoice.value must hash its FULL path (e.g.
  fnv1a64("Bass/Analog/Warm")), not just its own name, or two different
  parents with a same-named child collide.
- Only the immediate parent's scope value is ever needed by list_at, not
  the whole ancestor chain.
